section.subsection:
Static Skill Values DCs
When using Static Skill we do not bother to roll the skill die, instead we assume that the die rolled a 10 and calculate the skill value as per usual. So the Static Skill is 10 plus the Rank of the Ability being used plus any shifts/modifiers.
For Static Checks the Fate Value is borrowed from the opposing dice roll and used only for the purposes of triggering actions.
Static Checks are used by the GM for antagonists in order to save time. Players should use the Roll Dice method.
Imagine that on the goblin's turn he makes a Sword Strike 4 attack on Dourli, with no shifts. So Dourli has to beat the Goblin's Static Skill Value of 13 on his Defence roll.
